{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Reconstruct recovered/ by applying base.tar, day2.tar, and day3.tar in the order documented by chain.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"chain.txt directly shows the required order. The executor extracted the base into staging, applied day 2 and its deletion manifest, then day 3 and its deletion manifest before publishing the staging tree as recovered/.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8b57f4563ec6446d","cmd-055df5cb440e4821","cmd-a08219624a704243","cmd-310d286a27284d46","cmd-2a3229c3166e435e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Make recovered/ represent the end-of-day-3 workspace, including deletions and the latest versions of changed files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The published tree contains exactly dispatch.txt and retain.txt. dispatch.txt matches day3.tar and contains dispatch=Wednesday; retain.txt matches base.tar. obsolete.txt, route.txt, and deletions.txt are absent. The same state was observed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1222fd156699487b","cmd-310d286a27284d46","cmd-2a3229c3166e435e","cmd-9f1de8d296ab4fc0"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve all recovery media and the ordering recorded in chain.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final and post-restart chain contents remain base.tar, day2.tar, day3.tar. SHA-256 hashes for chain.txt and all three archives match the preparation baseline, directly showing that the media and ordering were preserved.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-41b937cacf6e4437","cmd-9f1de8d296ab4fc0"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 were unchanged from the fixed pre-executor snapshot through the post-restart state. The installed GNU tar 1.35 successfully performed the reconstruction, and package health remained intact.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-575d52ad04bb439a","cmd-9f1de8d296ab4fc0","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The staging directory creation, archive extraction, manifest-driven deletions, and final rename were directly necessary to construct and publish recovered/ (cmd-055df5cb440e4821, cmd-a08219624a704243, cmd-310d286a27284d46, cmd-2a3229c3166e435e). The scheduled reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol (cmd-c49cb9a0e4d3424b); it was bounded and followed by a different boot identity, healthy services, intact data and media, no failed units, and no abandoned staging directory. Lifecycle differences are normal reboot-generated PID and systemd-private-directory changes, not residue. Package health, listeners, and failed-service state remained healthy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-055df5cb440e4821","cmd-a08219624a704243","cmd-310d286a27284d46","cmd-2a3229c3166e435e","cmd-41b937cacf6e4437","cmd-c49cb9a0e4d3424b","cmd-47157e133b9f4446","cmd-9f1de8d296ab4fc0","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence. The recovered tree accurately represents end of day 3, the archives and chain order are unchanged, and the original RHEL release and kernel remain installed. The mandatory node1 restart protocol is complete: it records a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, independently corroborated boot-ID change, and recovered service, data, media, and system state.","limitations":[]}
